arter": "2017-10-01", "series": "SE", "late_delivery_rate": 0.23529411764705882, "orders": 68}, {"quarter": "2018-01-01", "series": "SE", "late_delivery_rate": 0.27450980392156865, "orders": 53}, {"quarter": "2018-04-01", "series": "SE", "late_delivery_rate": 0.17391304347826086, "orders": 50}, {"quarter": "2018-07-01", "series": "SE", "late_delivery_rate": 0.04081632653061224, "orders": 50}]}]}], "answer": "Alagoas (AL) has had the worst late-delivery rate, at **21.4%** of delivered orders, against a national rate of about 6.8%. It is getting better. Most of the problem came from a spike in late 2017 and early 2018, which has since eased [1][3].\n\n| Worst states, Sep 2016 to Aug 2018 | Late rate |\n|---|---|\n| AL | 21.4% |\n| MA | 17.4% |\n| SE | 15.2% |\n| PI | 13.9% |\n| CE | 13.8% |\n\n- Nationally, the rate rose from **3.4%** in Q3 2017 to **12.9%** in Q1 2018, then fell to 4.2% in Q2 2018 and 4.8% in Jul to Aug 2018 [3].\n- RJ is the biggest state on the list: 27.3% in Q1 2018, down to 4.2% [2].\n- MA is still at 13% in Jul to Aug 2018, and AL at 11% [2].\n\nCaveats: Sep and Oct 2018 are left out because the data tapers off, so Q3 2018 covers only Jul to Aug. Orders still undelivered at the cutoff may make that quarter look better than it is. The small states have fewer than 100 orders per quarter, so their numbers swing a lot.", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "role": "analyst", "source": "olist", "at": "2026-10-11T23:38:16.109Z", "secs": 23, "usage": {"in": 21786, "out": 2037, "cache": 18237}}]}